* '''Phase 1 — pilot (1 tile). Completed 2026-05-13.''' Tile <code>high-park-swansea-sw-se</code> — a depth-2 quadrant of the High Park-Swansea neighbourhood, bbox <code>(43.633436, -79.480592, 43.639157, -79.469502)</code>, 252 source candidates pre-conflation. 176 uploaded as [https://www.openstreetmap.org/changeset/182585291 changeset 182585291] (source snapshot #42), 72 skipped (range housenumbers), 4 manually rejected. End-to-end human review by the maintainer; the 8 candidates flagged by any check received explicit operator decisions in the review UI (4 approve, 4 reject), and the AUTO_APPROVED queue was surveyed by eye before upload was triggered. One-week hold observed before Phase 2.
* '''Phase 2 + Phase 3 — citywide rollout. Completed 2026-05-28.''' All 1,296 non-pilot tiles processed one at a time over thirteen working days (2026-05-13 → 2026-05-28). 1,297 production changesets total (including the pilot): [https://www.openstreetmap.org/changeset/182585291 182585291] through [https://www.openstreetmap.org/changeset/183305851 183305851], all under the [https://www.openstreetmap.org/user/skfd%20imports/history skfd imports] account. Aggregate per the local tool DB: ~449,052 addresses uploaded, ~310,596 skipped (~100k MATCH already in OSM + ~207k MISSING-but-deduped intra-source siblings + ~3.5k range housenumbers), ~9,221 operator-rejected at review time (the bulk being MATCH_FAR candidates where the operator judged the match real or the geometry wrong). 19 candidates remain in <code>REVIEW_PENDING</code> as the operator's intentional defer-pile; the closeout report enumerates them. Day-by-day surprises, recurring failure modes, and the running list of city-side data bugs caught during review are recorded in [https://github.com/skfd/toronto-2-address-import/blob/main/blog.md blog.md].
