* '''Phase 5 — continuous maintenance. Ongoing since 2026-06-05.''' No end date. See [[#Continuous maintenance|§ Continuous maintenance]].

=== Post-import follow-ups (scoped separately) ===

* '''Per-node <code>source</code> → <code>addr:source</code> rewrite — investigated, not pursued.''' The per-node attribution tag the rollout wrote (<code>source=City of Toronto Open Data</code>) is better expressed as <code>addr:source</code> — it sources the address, sits more cleanly in the <code>addr:*</code> namespace, and survives merges into building polygons without ambiguity. '''New nodes have written <code>addr:source</code> since 2026-08-27''' (see § Tagging plan), so the backlog stopped growing. Rewriting the ~449k rollout nodes was tested in a read-only pilot and '''dropped on 2026-06-03'''. The tag value is not this import's signature but a long-standing community convention — roughly 1,580 Toronto ways carry it, including building footprints tagged by other mappers years before this import — so a sweep by tag value would rewrite other people's edits, and only the nodes the upload manifest enumerates are provably ours. Even limited to those it is an automated edit over hundreds of thousands of objects with no per-object human review, which the [[Automated Edits code of conduct|Automated Edits code of conduct]] requires documented community consensus for — a disproportionate cost for a cosmetic key change. Evidence and pilot findings: [https://github.com/skfd/address-importer-friend/blob/main/future-work/source-tag-rewrite.md future-work/source-tag-rewrite.md]. Should it ever be revisited it starts with a forum thread, not with a changeset. The changeset-level <code>source</code> tag and the proposal's § Tagging plan text are not changed retroactively — the 2026-08-27 change is a forward-only correction to the tag written on new nodes.
* '''MapRoulette challenge for unanchored OSM buildings''' (~1,580 elements with <code>addr:housenumber</code> but no <code>addr:street</code>/<code>addr:place</code>/<code>addr:housename</code>) — already referenced under § Deferred work as the durable resolution of the third acknowledged duplicate-creation path. Sketch in [https://github.com/skfd/address-importer-friend/blob/main/future-work/no-anchor-osm-buildings.md future-work/no-anchor-osm-buildings.md].
* '''<code>addr:interpolation</code> cleanup mapping party''' — local-mapper-organised effort, separate forum thread, out of scope for this tool. Mentioned here only so reviewers can locate the cross-references.

Upload rate target is '''≤1 changeset per minute''' by manual cadence (the <code>upload.changesets_per_minute</code> config value is advisory — uploads are operator-triggered per run, not throttled by the tool). One run uploads as one changeset, and the tile design above keeps each run at 250–750 source addresses, so changeset size is bounded by the tile rather than a separate cap. The practical schedule is dominated by human review of the queue, not by upload throughput.

